---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
import Header from "../components/Header.astro";
import Footer from "../components/Footer.astro";
---

<Layout
  title="Privacy — Parley"
  description="What the hosted site at parleyprotocol.com collects and why: standard GA4 page-view and click-event analytics plus Microsoft Clarity session recordings with all text masked, both loaded only after you accept, no ads, no data resale, no tracking in the self-hosted core."
  path="/privacy/"
>
  <div class="mx-auto flex min-h-screen max-w-[720px] flex-col px-6 md:px-16">
    <Header />

    <main class="flex-1 pb-16">
      <h1 class="font-display text-3xl tracking-[-0.02em] text-ink">Privacy</h1>
      <p class="mt-1.5 text-[12.5px] text-subtle">Last updated 2026-11-23</p>

      <p class="mt-8 text-[15px]/[24px] text-muted">
        Parley itself — the protocol and the code in{" "}
        <a
          href="https://github.com/5uper0/parley"
          target="_blank"
          rel="noopener"
          class="text-indigo underline decoration-hairline underline-offset-2 hover:decoration-indigo"
          >github.com/5uper0/parley</a
        > — collects nothing. It is a zero-dependency Python library and a self-hosted
        demo; if you <code
          class="rounded-[5px] border border-hairline bg-surface px-[5px] py-px font-mono text-[0.92em]"
          >docker run</code
        > it locally or on your own infrastructure, no data leaves your machine and there
        is no telemetry, ever.
      </p>

      <div class="my-6 rounded-[14px] border border-hairline bg-surface px-5 py-[18px]">
        <p class="text-[15px]/[24px] text-muted">
          <strong class="text-ink">The hosted site at parleyprotocol.com (homepage and demo) is different</strong>{" "}
          — it uses Google Analytics (GA4) and Microsoft Clarity so we can tell whether the
          site is reaching anyone worth talking to. Neither loads until you choose
          Accept in the banner. Until then the page makes no request to Google or
          Microsoft and sets no analytics cookie.
        </p>
      </div>

      <h2 class="mt-8 mb-3 text-sm font-semibold text-muted">
        What's collected
      </h2>
      <ul class="list-disc space-y-1.5 pl-5">
        <li class="text-[14.5px] text-muted">
          Only after you accept: standard GA4 page views and browser/device metadata (the
          same as most websites). GA4 sets the cookies <code
            class="rounded-[5px] border border-hairline bg-surface px-[5px] py-px font-mono text-[0.92em]"
            >_ga</code
          > and <code
            class="rounded-[5px] border border-hairline bg-surface px-[5px] py-px font-mono text-[0.92em]"
            >_ga_*</code
          >.
        </li>
        <li class="text-[14.5px] text-muted">
          Only after you accept: Microsoft Clarity (free) records how pages are used:
          clicks, scrolls and page layout. Text on the page is masked in the recording
          and nothing you type into the demo is captured. Once you accept, Clarity sets
          the cookies <code
            class="rounded-[5px] border border-hairline bg-surface px-[5px] py-px font-mono text-[0.92em]"
            >_clck</code
          > and <code
            class="rounded-[5px] border border-hairline bg-surface px-[5px] py-px font-mono text-[0.92em]"
            >_clsk</code
          > so it can link the page views of one visit. Microsoft processes this data
          under its own privacy terms.
        </li>
        <li class="text-[14.5px] text-muted">
          Only after you accept: a handful of click events scoped to this page: running a scenario, clicking
          verify, clicking the Arena "join the beta" link, or clicking through to
          GitHub, Discussions, or LinkedIn. No content you type into the demo (party
          names, preferences) is sent — the events log that a button was clicked, not
          what the decision was.
        </li>
      </ul>

      <h2 class="mt-8 mb-3 text-sm font-semibold text-muted">
        What's not collected
      </h2>
      <ul class="list-disc space-y-1.5 pl-5">
        <li class="text-[14.5px] text-muted">No account, no email, no login — the demo doesn't ask for either.</li>
        <li class="text-[14.5px] text-muted">No advertising identifiers, no ad network, no retargeting pixels.</li>
        <li class="text-[14.5px] text-muted">No data is sold, or used for anything beyond understanding demo traffic. It is shared only with the two analytics processors named above.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2 class="mt-8 mb-3 text-sm font-semibold text-muted">
        Your options
      </h2>
      <p class="text-[14.5px]/[24px] text-muted">
        The banner offers Reject and Accept with equal weight. Your choice is stored in
        this browser (localStorage key <code
          class="rounded-[5px] border border-hairline bg-surface px-[5px] py-px font-mono text-[0.92em]"
          >parley-consent</code
        >) and is not sent anywhere. If you reject, nothing from Google or Microsoft
        loads. You can change your choice at any time:
      </p>
      <p class="mt-3">
        <button
          type="button"
          data-consent-open
          class="inline-flex min-h-11 cursor-pointer items-center rounded-full border border-hairline bg-surface px-5 text-[14px] text-ink transition-colors hover:border-indigo"
        >
          Cookie settings
        </button>
      </p>
      <p class="mt-4 text-[14.5px]/[24px] text-muted">
        Any ad-blocker or tracking-protection extension that blocks Google Analytics or
        Microsoft Clarity will block them too — the demo works identically either way, nothing is gated
        on analytics. For zero analytics of any kind, run the demo yourself: <code
          class="rounded-[5px] border border-hairline bg-surface px-[5px] py-px font-mono text-[0.92em]"
          >docker build -t parley . && docker run --rm -p 8080:8080 parley</code
        >{" "}
        (see the{" "}
        <a
          href="https://github.com/5uper0/parley#see-it-in-30-seconds"
          target="_blank"
          rel="noopener"
          class="text-indigo underline decoration-hairline underline-offset-2 hover:decoration-indigo"
          >README</a
        >).
      </p>

      <h2 class="mt-8 mb-3 text-sm font-semibold text-muted">
        Contact
      </h2>
      <p class="text-[14.5px]/[24px] text-muted">
        Questions —{" "}
        <a
          href="https://github.com/5uper0/parley/discussions"
          target="_blank"
          rel="noopener"
          class="text-indigo underline decoration-hairline underline-offset-2 hover:decoration-indigo"
          >open a GitHub Discussion</a
        >.
      </p>
    </main>
  </div>

  <Footer />
</Layout>
